 "story": {
  "title": "A landscape that becomes a lake",
  "lede": "The haors of northeastern Bangladesh are shallow basins that fill with monsoon water every year, turning farmland into an inland sea.",
  "body": [
   "Calm water reflects the radar away like a mirror, so flooded land goes dark in both channels: the Vanish. In this box, about 21,600 hectares looked like open water in June and 25,200 on September 10. By late September most had drained.",
   "On August 17 the water lit up instead. Wind ripples roughen a water surface and send the pulse back: one of radar's known blind spots, and a reason one pass is never the whole story."
  ],
